  "response_complete": true,
  "response_text": "Handling recurrent headaches with light sensitivity without giving a diagnosis involves several steps:\n\n1. **Assess the Symptoms**: Note down the frequency, duration, and intensity of the headaches. Also, observe if there are any triggers that seem to cause the headaches, such as certain foods, stress, or specific activities.\n\n2. **Consult a Healthcare Professional**: It's important to consult a healthcare provider, such as a neurologist or a primary care physician, to get a proper diagnosis. They can rule out other potential causes and provide appropriate treatment.\n\n3. **Medication Review**: Discuss any medications you are currently taking, including over-the-counter pain relievers, as some can exacerbate light sensitivity. Your doctor may suggest alternatives or adjust your current medications.\n\n4. **Light Therapy**: Depending on the severity and type of light sensitivity, you might need to avoid bright lights or use specialized glasses that filter out certain wavelengths of light.\n\n5. **Lifestyle Adjustments**: Incorporate lifestyle changes that can help manage headaches. This might include stress management techniques, regular exercise, and maintaining a healthy diet.\n\n6. **Pain Management**: If headaches are severe, your doctor might prescribe stronger pain medications. However, always follow the prescribed dosage and consult your doctor if you experience side effects.\n\n7. **Follow-Up**: Regular follow-ups with your healthcare provider are crucial to monitor your condition and adjust treatments as necessary.\n\nRemember, it's important to get a proper diagnosis to understand the underlying cause of your headaches and to receive appropriate treatment.",
